---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="BOOM Stack - Ready to Build">
  <h1>🚀 BOOM Stack Template</h1>
  <p>Your HTML-first app starts here. Clone this template and build fast.</p>

  <h2>Example: Dynamic Content with HTMX</h2>
  <p>Click the button to see HTMX in action - it fetches HTML from the server and swaps it in.</p>

  <button
    hx-get="/api/example"
    hx-target="#result"
    hx-swap="innerHTML"
  >
    Click me
  </button>

  <div id="result" style="margin-top: 1rem;"></div>

  <hr />

  <h2>What's Next?</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 2;">
    <li>Edit <code>src/pages/index.astro</code> to customize this page</li>
    <li>Add your API routes in <code>src/pages/api/</code></li>
    <li>Create components in <code>src/components/</code></li>
    <li>Use <code>db()</code> from <code>src/lib/db.ts</code> to query MongoDB</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Quick Tips</h2>
  <ul style="line-height: 2;">
    <li><strong>HTMX</strong>: Add <code>hx-get</code>, <code>hx-post</code> to any element</li>
    <li><strong>MongoDB</strong>: Already connected, just import <code>db</code></li>
    <li><strong>Deploy</strong>: Run <code>docker build</code> or deploy to Vercel/Netlify</li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <p><small>
    Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> +
    <a href="https://bun.sh">Bun</a> +
    <a href="https://htmx.org">HTMX</a> +
    <a href="https://mongodb.com">MongoDB</a>
  </small></p>
</Base>

<style>
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  a {
    color: #3b82f6;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
